{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>That the dwellers of the ends fear</b> — opposite the Temple." "<b>Your signs</b> — and they are the mighty deeds of the rain, like: \"who does great things beyond number\"." "<b>And the meaning of מוצאי בקר</b> — the signs that go out, seen in the morning and evening; because of them the children of men sing, and so the word תרנין will govern two verbs. And R. Moses said: that the beginning of day and night, where the end of this is the beginning of that, are the cause of the singing."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 65, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:32:44.482255976Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}